import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'stale-hit':('A stale entry one past the count names the giant','A hill giant stands adjacent to the Warrior while the Teleport Other exclusion list holds one real entry (not the giant) and a stale leftover one past the count — the state a longer earlier evaluation leaves. The original reads that stale entry, matches the giant and rates its danger as zero; the correction reads only the real entries and rates the danger 179.'),
 'in-list':('Control: the giant genuinely is in the list','With the giant actually excluded (a real entry), both versions rate the danger zero. The complete logs are byte-identical.'),
 'empty':('Control: empty list','With no exclusions at all, both versions rate the giant\'s danger 179. The complete logs are byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/tpreader-250 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('SETUP n=','setup'),('DANGER ','danger'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The Teleport Other exclusion list read one entry too many</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native danger scores</p><h1>The Teleport Other exclusion list read one entry too many</h1><p>While scoring a Teleport Other, the Borg keeps a list of monsters it plans to banish, so their danger is not counted twice. The exclusion loop in the per-monster danger routine ran one entry past that list — into a slot holding a stale index from an earlier, longer evaluation. Any monster whose index happened to sit in that slot had its danger dropped entirely: an adjacent giant could be rated harmless while the Borg decided whether to teleport away. The correction reads only the real entries.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The list</button><button data-step="1">The danger score</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>With the giant genuinely in the list, both versions still exclude its danger; with an empty list, both count it. Those two complete logs match byte for byte, so the correction changes only the stale-read case.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior, seed 1000, glowing constructed arena, lit torch, an awake hill giant adjacent to the Borg (measured danger 179). The exclusion list is set directly in the state a longer earlier Teleport Other evaluation leaves behind (one real entry, one stale leftover past the count) — recorded as a fixture intervention. The production per-monster danger routine runs unmodified; no damage or survival claim beyond this one score.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/250">issue250</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}
function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`List entries: ${d.setup?d.setup.n:'?'}, giant index ${data['stale-hit'].before.setup?data['stale-hit'].before.setup.idx1:'?'} in stale-hit.`:`Danger score: ${d.danger?d.danger.danger:'?'}.`;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'The list state before the danger routine runs.':'What the giant rates as danger to the Borg.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?(d.danger&&d.danger.danger>0?'Counts the giant as dangerous.':'Rates the giant as harmless (danger 0).'):'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}
document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='stale-hit'?'The original lets a stale list entry erase the giant\\'s danger; the correction counts it.':'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}
select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
